{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And it shall be heard</b> Three times in the Masorah: this one, and the other two: כל אשר דבר ה' נעשה ונשמע, and ונשמע פתגם המלך. And this is what we say in Megillah: Rabba said: reading the Megillah and Tefillah — reading the Megillah takes precedence; reading the Megillah and Avodah — reading the Megillah takes precedence. And this is כל אשר דבר ה' נעשה ונשמע, which is Tefillah and Avodah, for it is written of it: ונשמע קולו. ונשמע פתגם המלך — and this is reading the Megillah; and it is adjacent to כי רבה היא, evidently it takes precedence more, and Rabba also said it:" "<b>And when he goes out</b> Two times in the Masorah: this one, and the other: והיו את המלך בבואו ובצאתו, regarding Joash in Chronicles, where they would guard him lest they kill him. And this is: ובצאתו — and he shall not die:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The word ת\"ת is taken as an abbreviation for תפלה, paired with עבודה, following the Talmudic passage in b. Megillah 18a-b; resolved per context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:41.321287009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}